  reproduces the aqueous acid the lactate ions are referred to (their hfAq are that value plus the Table 6
  ionisation enthalpies).  The dissociated route is the lactate family (see species/ and chemistry/).

  NOT carried: the aqueous heat capacity `Cp`.  No work in hand prints it for this acid, so the cp_aq rung
  refuses by name when a duty reaches the sensible heat of the solution; the formation-level (298.15 K)
  balance is complete.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

solute      lacticAcid;
