        //  as a second opinion on this ion at 25 C; it is a compilation and is not this value's origin.
        D0
        {
            source        "R. A. Robinson and R. H. Stokes, Electrolyte Solutions, 2nd ed., Butterworths, London, 1959, read in the Russian translation (R. Robinson, R. Stoks, Rastvory elektrolitov, ed. A. N. Frumkin, Izdatel'stvo Inostrannoi Literatury, Moskva, 1963), Appendix 6.1 (Predel'naya ekvivalentnaya elektroprovodnost' ionov pri 25 C v vode), p. 534 (PDF p. 531 of the folder copy), row Propionat (propionate): lambda0 = 35.8 S cm2/eq at 25 C; the book's own literature reference for the row: no. 18, D. Belcher, J. Am. Chem. Soc. 60, 2744 (1938)";
            origin        literature;
            method        "read at the page image, 2026-11-15 (DEV.md 4c C403): lambda0 = 35.8 S cm2/eq (x 1e-4 = 0.00358 S m2/eq), converted by the Nernst relation D = R T lambda0 / (|z| F^2) with R = 8.314462618 J/mol/K, F = 96485.33212 C/mol, T = 298.15 K (RT/F^2 = 2.662848e-07), |z| = 1, to 9.533e-10 m2/s";
            reviewStatus  interim;
            notes         "The same conversion applied to the book's Na+ row (lambda0 50.10) gives 1.334e-09 m2/s, +0.3 % against Li & Gregory's 1.33e-9 for Na+ (the conductance and tracer routes differ by that much).  No page of the English edition was seen: every page named here is the Russian translation's. A second compiled table (named in the comment above) gives 9.53e-10 m2/s for this ion at 25 C (-0.03 %).";
        }
    }
}
