    provenance
    {
        //  Cross-check, entering no value: the CRC Handbook of Chemistry and Physics, 82nd ed., table
        //  'Ionic Conductivity and Diffusion at Infinite Dilution' (PDF pp. 304-306 of the folder copy), read at its page
        //  as a second opinion on this ion at 25 C; it is a compilation and is not this value's origin.
        D0
        {
            source        "R. A. Robinson and R. H. Stokes, Electrolyte Solutions, 2nd ed., Butterworths, London, 1959, read in the Russian translation (R. Robinson, R. Stoks, Rastvory elektrolitov, ed. A. N. Frumkin, Izdatel'stvo Inostrannoi Literatury, Moskva, 1963), Appendix 6.1 (Predel'naya ekvivalentnaya elektroprovodnost' ionov pri 25 C v vode), p. 534 (PDF p. 531 of the folder copy), row Butirat (butyrate): lambda0 = 32.6 S cm2/eq at 25 C; the book's own literature reference for the row: no. 18, D. Belcher, J. Am. Chem. Soc. 60, 2744 (1938)";
            origin        literature;
            method        "read at the page image, 2026-11-15 (DEV.md 4c C403): lambda0 = 32.6 S cm2/eq (x 1e-4 = 0.00326 S m2/eq), converted by the Nernst relation D = R T lambda0 / (|z| F^2) with R = 8.314462618 J/mol/K, F = 96485.33212 C/mol, T = 298.15 K (RT/F^2 = 2.662848e-07), |z| = 1, to 8.681e-10 m2/s";
            reviewStatus  interim;
